  (footprint "famicart:RPi_Pico_SMD_Short" (layer "F.Cu")
    (tstamp 9082f2e4-ba96-4b81-995a-22b141b86e1e)
    (at 26.7 12 90)
    (descr "Raspberry Pi Pico / Pico 2 module, castellated SMD pads (40 + 3 debug) + USB test points TP1/TP2/TP3 per Pico 2 datasheet Fig.5. USB connector at -Y (top). -- SHORT PADS: main-board pads end 0.4 mm outside the module (instead of 1.0) so the module can sit close to the card-edge shoulder and shell ribs (rev F2). Castellation pads sit on the datasheet pad line (first pad 1.37 mm from the module end). Pads 44-46 = TP1-TP3, TP4-TP7 and the USB shell pads A-D are no-net copper under the module, without paste: they keep tracks and vias away from the module's exposed test points (TP6 BOOTSEL, TP7 1V1) and USB shell legs. The module is hand-soldered at the castellations.")
